From 891f931ec446a719b89d3f89cf0e1de01ee3f39d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eric Duprey <509630+destinal@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 12:51:04 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 01/18] Support all OSC 9;4 progress states

Konsole treated the indeterminate state (OSC 9;4;3) the same as hiding
progress and ignored the error and paused states. Programs such as
Claude Code report a running turn as indeterminate progress, so the start
of a turn looked the same as its end.

Progress now carries a state: normal, error, indeterminate or paused.
Tabs draw error in the negative color, paused in the neutral color, and
indeterminate as a segment sliding across the bar. The error and paused
states keep the last percentage when they omit one. The taskbar entry
has no indeterminate state, so it stays hidden for that case as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
